<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Land Ordinance of Vladislaus II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1500">1500</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Vladislav Land Ordinance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Land Ordinance of Vladislaus II was a code of the land law of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>, issued in 1500 under King Vladislaus II Jagiellon. Drawn up by the estates, it confirmed the dominance of the lords and knights in the diet and the courts and restricted the political rights of the royal towns. It remained the basis of Bohemian law until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renewed-land-ordinance">Renewed Land Ordinance</a> of 1627.</p></div>
